From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm5: hand the prompt tail state from prefill to decode

In the W4A16 + DFlash2 PD pair LMCache only stores whole 5120-token chunks:
the KDA recurrent state is checkpointed at block boundaries, so the decode
engine recomputed the last partial chunk (prompt length mod 5120, up to 5119
tokens; 4600 tokens / ~1.8 s at 107k) on the decode GPUs.

With VLLM_GLM53_PD_TAIL=1 the prefill engine, after its prompt pass, packs
each PP rank's end-of-prompt state - KDA recurrent + conv state, the partial
MLA / indexer / kpool tail, the DFlash2 drafter window and the last hidden /
aux states - into GPU chunks of a separate LMCache namespace and stores them
with LMCache's own STORE/RETRIEVE + CUDA IPC (L1/L2/LRU as usual; LMCache is
not modified). A small generation record, published only once all four
shards are stored, ties them to the exact prompt, cache_salt and model
configuration. The decode engine loads the ordinary prefix chunks, then the
tail into request-private pages.

The loaded KDA state has already consumed the last prompt token, so the
decode engine must not replay it: its first step is sample-only - no target
forward; LM head, sampler and DFlash proposal run on the restored hidden
state with the decode request's own sampling parameters. Target replay is 0
tokens. Loaded state, first-step logits and draft candidates match a local
full prefill bitwise.

Anything unsupported (one side without the switch, missing tail or prefix,
multimodal, LoRA, prompt logprobs, preempted requests, prompts that are a
multiple of 5120) keeps the old path. Scope: PP4/TP1/DP1, mamba align,
folded aux, DFlash2. The LMCache server needs --supported-transfer-mode=auto
for the generation record. Default off; VLLM_GLM53_OPT_PROFILE=default
enables it (it only acts with the LMCacheMPConnector).

